.TH FILE 1 "June 17, 2025" "file 5.47"
.SH NAME
file \- determine file type
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B file
.RB [ \-bcdEhiklLNnprsSvzZ0 ]
.RB [ \-\-apple ]
.RB [ \-\-extension ]
.RB [ \-\-mime-encoding ]
.RB [ \-\-mime-type ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR testname ]
.RB [ \-F
.IR separator ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR namefile ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR magicfiles ]
.RB [ \-P
.IR name=value ]
.I file ...
.br
.B file \-C
.RB [ \-m
.IR magicfiles ]
.br
.B file \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B file
5.47 classifies each operand using filesystem metadata, built-in structural
tests, and the compiled libmagic database
.IR /usr/share/misc/magic.mgc .
It recognizes executable and object formats, archives, filesystems,
documents, media, source code, scripts, encodings, and many other formats.
.PP
The database is mapped read-only and demand-paged.  Input is inspected through
bounded reads and positioned I/O; the descriptor's current offset is not
changed by libmagic.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b
Brief output: do not prepend the file name.
.TP
.B \-c
Check the syntax of a text magic file.
.TP
.B \-C
Compile a text magic file to
.BR .mgc .
.TP
.B \-d
Enable debugging output.
.TP
.BI \-e " testname"
Exclude a test.  Names include
.BR apptype ,
.BR ascii ,
.BR cdf ,
.BR compress ,
.BR csv ,
.BR elf ,
.BR encoding ,
.BR json ,
.BR simh ,
.BR soft ,
and
.BR tar .
.TP
.B \-E
Treat filesystem errors as fatal classification errors.
.TP
.BI \-f " namefile"
Read file names, one per line, from
.IR namefile .
Use
.B -
for standard input.
.TP
.BI \-F " separator"
Use
.I separator
between the name and result.
.TP
.B \-h
Do not follow symbolic links.
.TP
.B \-i
Print MIME type and character encoding.
.TP
.B \-k
Continue after the first matching rule.
.TP
.B \-L
Follow symbolic links.
.TP
.B \-l
List magic rules in strength order.
.TP
.BI \-m " magicfiles"
Use the specified colon-separated magic paths.
.TP
.B \-N
Do not pad file names.
.TP
.B \-n
Flush output after every file.
.TP
.B \-p
Preserve access time.
.TP
.BI \-P " name=value"
Set a libmagic limit such as
.BR bytes ,
.BR encoding ,
.BR indir ,
.BR name ,
or
.BR regex .
.TP
.B \-r
Do not escape non-printing result bytes.
.TP
.B \-s
Read block and character devices.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the program and magic database versions.
.TP
.B \-z
Inspect the contents of compressed files when a matching decompressor is
available.
.TP
.B \-Z
Like
.BR \-z ,
but report only the uncompressed content type.
.TP
.B \-0
Terminate the file-name field with a NUL byte.
.TP
.B \-\-apple
Print Apple creator/type information.
.TP
.B \-\-extension
Print a slash-separated list of likely file-name extensions.
.TP
.B \-\-mime-type
Print only the MIME media type.
.TP
.B \-\-mime-encoding
Print only the MIME character encoding.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAGIC
Colon-separated path used instead of the default database.
.TP
.B POSIXLY_CORRECT
Follow symbolic links by default and use POSIX option processing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/misc/magic.mgc
Compiled magic database.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means every requested operation succeeded.  A non-zero status reports
an invalid option, an unreadable operand, an invalid database, or another
classification error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR strings (1),
.BR stat (2),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR pread (2)
